ssional rematch one of most-watched US House races", "source": "ABC11 News", "published": "2026-08-24T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 2.12, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 5.22, "poll_sd": 9.47, "poll_weight": 0.23, "fundamentals": {"margin": 4.88, "lean": -5.0, "environment": 7.9, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": -0.02}, "rating_margin": 0.28, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.33, "baseline_margin": 2.82, "analyst_adjustment": -0.32, "key_factors": ["Don Davis's incumbency and centrist record in a district redrawn to favor Republicans", "Prediction markets price Davis around 60% despite the district's R+5 lean", "Recent Democratic-sponsored polling shows Davis ahead 7 points", "Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean/Tilt R flip"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican-leaning district, but Davis's incumbency, strong cash position, and a fresh September poll showing a 7-point lead offset that lean, and markets price him near 60%. With ratings split between Tossup and Lean R, a narrow Democratic edge with wide uncertainty is the balanced call.", "watch": "A late wave of Republican outside spending or a national environment shift toward the GOP could flip this tossup district.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Don Davis (D) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 1st District was redrawn to lean Republican by about five points, setting up a rematch between incumbent Democrat Don Davis and Republican Laurie Buckhout. Davis has built a centrist record and holds a large cash advantage, with $3.6 million on hand versus Buckhout's $1.8 million, though she has drawn more outside support. A September poll from a Democratic sponsor showed Davis up 7 points, while earlier polls were tighter. Expert raters disagree: some call it a Tossup, others Lean or Tilt Republican with a flip expected. Prediction markets give Davis roughly a 60 percent chance of holding the seat. The race remains genuinely competitive, with Buckhout campaigning heavily on veterans issues and Trump's tax policy while Davis emphasizes health care and rural needs.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6957, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6748, "margin": 2.5}]}